  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116520",
      "title": "Using Lazy Loading & Routing to Lazy-load Services",
      "lectureOrder": 306,
      "videoOrder": 291,
      "sourceHash": "93ab72770579c2e6e78d633155a45395bc88a3df530a281f8a2535fe1930c453",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.24,
          "end": 1.8,
          "en": "So now that you know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.8,
          "end": 5.19,
          "en": "how to lazily load routes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.19,
          "end": 9.06,
          "en": "there's one last kind of related feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.06,
          "end": 11.82,
          "en": "that could also be interesting to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.82,
          "end": 15.99,
          "en": "and that would be lazy loading of services,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.99,
          "end": 16.833,
          "en": "you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.67,
          "end": 19.44,
          "en": "because in this application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.44,
          "end": 23.37,
          "en": "I got this TasksService,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.37,
          "end": 25.71,
          "en": "which is in the end only used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.71,
          "end": 28.563,
          "en": "by these task-related components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.82,
          "end": 32.58,
          "en": "Put in other words, this service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.58,
          "end": 36.39,
          "en": "and all the code that's imported into this service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.39,
          "end": 39.843,
          "en": "isn't needed when the application starts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.89,
          "end": 41.97,
          "en": "At the moment, however,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.97,
          "end": 44.52,
          "en": "it would always be loaded right at the start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.52,
          "end": 46.92,
          "en": "because we're providing this service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.92,
          "end": 50.13,
          "en": "in the application route injector,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.13,
          "end": 53.19,
          "en": "and this injector, as the name suggests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.19,
          "end": 57.39,
          "en": "is set up when the application is started,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.39,
          "end": 61.5,
          "en": "so therefore, what you could consider doing here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.5,
          "end": 64.65,
          "en": "is get rid of this configuration object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.65,
          "end": 67.32,
          "en": "you're passing to Injectable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.32,
          "end": 71.07,
          "en": "so that this service will actually not be provided",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.07,
          "end": 72.993,
          "en": "with the route injector anymore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.89,
          "end": 76.26,
          "en": "and, of course, if you do that and you save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.26,
          "end": 80.85,
          "en": "your application will break if you try to visit a user here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.85,
          "end": 83.223,
          "en": "if you try to load the data for the user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.45,
          "end": 87.3,
          "en": "but now the trick is to provide the service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.3,
          "end": 88.95,
          "en": "in a different way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 88.95,
          "end": 91.26,
          "en": "Specifically, you can go to this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 91.26,
          "end": 94.08,
          "en": "users.routes.ts file now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.08,
          "end": 96.78,
          "en": "and provide the service there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.78,
          "end": 100.17,
          "en": "You could add another route here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 100.17,
          "end": 105.12,
          "en": "which has an empty path and which has a children property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 105.12,
          "end": 109.32,
          "en": "so that you can wrap those routes that already existed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 109.32,
          "end": 110.82300000000001,
          "en": "with that route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 112.17,
          "end": 115.113,
          "en": "and I'm telling you why I'm doing that in just a second,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 116.13,
          "end": 119.67,
          "en": "so with that, I have this extra route here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 119.67,
          "end": 123.33,
          "en": "as a wrapper around all these task-related routes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 123.33,
          "end": 127.32,
          "en": "and I'm doing that because you can now go to that route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 127.32,
          "end": 130.77,
          "en": "and add the provider's property to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 130.77,
          "end": 133.743,
          "en": "You can add that on a route level as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 135,
          "end": 137.76,
          "en": "and when adding providers to a route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 137.76,
          "end": 141.27,
          "en": "all nested routes and the route to which you add it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 141.27,
          "end": 145.56,
          "en": "will have access to the providers defined here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 145.56,
          "end": 148.893,
          "en": "so to the services defined here, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 149.91,
          "end": 153.42000000000002,
          "en": "and therefore, now, we could add the TasksService here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 153.42000000000002,
          "end": 155.16,
          "en": "to this providers array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 155.16,
          "end": 158.823,
          "en": "and that would make it available to all the nested routes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 160.29,
          "end": 162.54,
          "en": "but since these routes here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 162.54,
          "end": 165.6,
          "en": "these user routes are loaded lazily,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 165.6,
          "end": 169.53,
          "en": "this service would now also be loaded and set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 169.53,
          "end": 171.483,
          "en": "by Angular lazily,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 172.35,
          "end": 175.29,
          "en": "and therefore, with that, if you save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 175.29,
          "end": 177.06,
          "en": "and if you click on a user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 177.06,
          "end": 179.97,
          "en": "you'll not be getting an error anymore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 179.97,
          "end": 182.52,
          "en": "but the TasksService code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 182.52,
          "end": 185.643,
          "en": "is now actually also loaded lazily,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 186.75,
          "end": 189.33,
          "en": "and that's just another useful tool",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 189.33,
          "end": 191.73,
          "en": "to have in your tool belt",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 191.73,
          "end": 194.49,
          "en": "because, of course, you sometimes have services",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 194.49,
          "end": 197.76,
          "en": "that must be available to the entire application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 197.76,
          "end": 200.76,
          "en": "and in that case, you can't lazy load them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 200.76,
          "end": 203.52,
          "en": "but if you have services that are only relevant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 203.52,
          "end": 207.84,
          "en": "to a subset of your components and routes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 207.84,
          "end": 211.77,
          "en": "you can absolutely consider lazy loading them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 211.77,
          "end": 213.51,
          "en": "by lazy loading them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 213.51,
          "end": 217.02,
          "en": "with help of this route providers array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 217.02,
          "end": 218.25,
          "en": "Of course, this alone",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 218.25,
          "end": 220.77,
          "en": "does not lazy load this service, though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 220.77,
          "end": 224.43,
          "en": "Instead, it does lead to this service being lazy loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 224.43,
          "end": 226.53,
          "en": "because the overall routes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 226.53,
          "end": 229.47,
          "en": "this overall array here, is loaded lazily",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 229.47,
          "end": 233.85,
          "en": "with help of this loadChildren property in our app routes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 233.85,
          "end": 236.15,
          "en": "but that's, therefore, something you could do.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
